    {
      "id": "GU-C149-bolish",
      "sequence": 7850,
      "title": "હું બોલીશ — the future, built on મળીશું",
      "headword": "…ીશ · …ીશું",
      "romanization": "-īś · -īśũ",
      "gloss": "I will, we will: the future is an ending, and maḷīśũ was the first one you owned",
      "script": "gujarati",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:4e73cbec8f9cb03a",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say I drank tea and I ate rice. Then the goodbye from the first week: કાલે મળીશું, see you tomorrow, word for word tomorrow we will meet."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: -ીશું, we will",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "મળીશું is મળ-, meet, plus -ીશું, we will. Gujarati needs no separate word for will: the future is an ending on the stem."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "આપણે કાલે મળીશું. — āpṇe kāle maḷīśũ. — We'll meet tomorrow. અમે ગુજરાતી બોલીશું. — ame gujarātī bolīśũ. — We will speak Gujarati."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: -ીશ, I will",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Take the last -ું off and you have I will:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હું ગુજરાતી બોલીશ. — hũ gujarātī bolīś. — I will speak Gujarati."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The familiar you takes the same form in the standard language: તું બોલીશ, you will speak. There is no copula and no gender: a man and a woman both say હું બોલીશ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The -શ of these endings is usually traced to the old Sanskrit future, the -iṣya- of kariṣyati, \"will do\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "hũ bolīś, ame bolīśũ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *hũ bolīś*, *ame bolīśũ*]"
            },
            {
